From bcfbccf73b68320b0e080b6376ead418cbbe063d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 21:39:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Harden livekit-token auth, remove 22 orphaned edge functions

Security fix:
- livekit-token previously trusted client-supplied roomName and
  participantName with no auth check at all, meaning any caller could
  get a join token for any room (including private ones) under any
  identity string. It now requires a valid Supabase session, derives
  the participant's identity from their own profile server-side, and
  checks the target room's type/membership before issuing a token.
- Updated the one frontend caller (LiveRoom.tsx via the livekit
  adapter) to match: identity is no longer sent by the client.

Cleanup:
- Deleted 22 edge functions confirmed unused by any
  supabase.functions.invoke() call in the frontend, including 5 that
  were unimplemented stubs ('// TODO: Implement logic') and several
  duplicate camelCase/snake_case pairs of the same operation.
- Deleted scripts/scaffold_edge_functions.js, the generator that
  produced those stub functions, so it can't regenerate them.
- Merged supabase/functions/shared/ into the Supabase-idiomatic
  _shared/ folder (two shared-code folders existed; only one was
  actually imported by any surviving function).
- Removed a stray 0-byte root-level schema.sql (the real schema lives
  in database/schema.sql).

No functions still in use were modified except livekit-token.
tsc --noEmit passes with zero errors after these changes.
